-- MUS-012-crystal-voltage
-- Created 2026-03-13

Good news and bad news. Most real-world TidalCycles techno uses **custom sample packs** (ghostchamb3r uses `BMDrums`, Tyler McLaughlin uses custom `drumz` functions) — nothing I found runs cleanly on a standard SuperDirt install.

**Best actual find:** [Tyler McLaughlin's live code repo](https://github.com/TylerMclaughlin/tidalcycles_code) — 300+ sessions, includes `2022_05_11_techno_likatsstlelakatsstle` and `2023_06_05_four_part_techno_edo19`. Worth browsing for inspiration, but needs his custom tooling.

**What I'd suggest:** I can write you a proper Berlin techno piece right now using only the standard samples listed in the quick ref — it'll actually run. Based on the patterns I found researching, something with:

- 4/4 kick with groove modulation
- 16th-note hat pattern with panning
- Acid bassline with resonance LFO
- Dark pad chords
- Techstab lead with `every 4`

Want me to generate that? Just say **"write me a berlin techno track"** and I'll output the code.

---

**Sources:**
- [Prepared Code with ghostchamb3r — TidalCycles Blog](https://tidalcycles.org/blog/blog_topic_ghostchamb3r/)
- [Tyler McLaughlin's TidalCycles live code repo](https://github.com/TylerMclaughlin/tidalcycles_code)
- [TidalCycles Workshop](https://tidalcycles.org/docs/patternlib/tutorials/workshop/)
- [Live Coding Techno With Strudel — Hackaday](https://hackaday.com/2025/10/16/live-coding-techno-with-strudel/)
setcps (133/60/4)

-- d1: kick (four on the floor, hardkick variant)
d1 $ s "bd:2*4" # gain 1.1 # lpf 200

-- d2: clap/snare on 2 and 4
d2 $ s "~ cp ~ cp" # gain 0.7 # room 0.2 # sz 0.6

-- d3: closed hats, driving 16ths with groove
d3 $ every 4 (jux rev) $ s "hh*16" # gain (slow 4 $ range 0.4 0.75 sine) # hpf 8000

-- d4: open hat on offbeats + industrial perc
d4 $ s "~ oh:2 ~ oh:2" # gain 0.6 # room 0.15
   |+ s "industrial:3? industrial:7? ~ ~" # gain 0.45

-- d5: reese bass, dark and minimal
d5 $ note (slow 2 $ "0 ~ ~ 0 ~ ~ 0 ~") $ s "reese"
   # detune 0.2 # lpf 400 # gain 0.9 # room 0.1

-- d6: subbass locking with kick
d6 $ note "0 ~ ~ ~ 0 ~ ~ ~" $ s "subbass"
   # gain 1.0 # lpf 120

-- d9: acid line, slow filter sweep
d9 $ every 8 (fast 2) $ note "0 ~ 3 ~ 5 ~ 3 ~" $ s "acid"
   # resonance 0.6
   # lpf (slow 8 $ range 300 3500 sine)
   # gain 0.75

-- d10: dark pad, wide and sparse
d10 $ slow 4 $ note "<[0,7] [0,5] [3,7] [2,5]>" $ s "darkpad"
    # detune 0.3 # room 0.8 # sz 0.9
    # lpf 1800 # gain 0.45 # delay 0.3 # delaytime 0.25

-- d11: metallic hi-hat texture (synth)
d11 $ every 3 degrade $ s "metallic*8"
    # gain (slow 2 $ range 0.2 0.55 sine)
    # hpf 9000 # pan (slow 7 $ range 0.2 0.8 sine)
